<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hittite laws</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hittite legal code</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hittite laws are a collection of legal provisions from the Hittite kingdom, preserved on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuneiform">cuneiform</a> tablets from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusa">Hattusa</a>. They cover matters such as property, family, agriculture and crime, often favouring compensation over harsh physical punishment. They are a key source for governance in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hittite-laws.jpg" alt="Hittite laws" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mx. Granger · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hittite_Cuneiform_Tablet-_Legal_Deposition(%3F).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
